Tourists in Portugal terrified after low flight of military jet over beach
Tourists who relished the sun's rays in Aveir, Portugal, were scared to death
The P-3C Orion, a Portuguese Air Force, flew incredibly low
The Air Force said it was a training flight, insisting there was no threat to security
When the low-flying jet descended over the crowded beach, the frightened tourists panicked.
Dramatic footage shows a military plane getting almost to the touch of sunny people on a sandy beach near Aveiro in northern Portugal.
Tourists began to rise after they were disturbed by the noise of the engines of the jet plane, without seeing what would emerge from the clouds.
The incident occurred yesterday afternoon on Costa Nova near Aveiro.
Daniel Fernandes, one of several holidaymakers who posted videotapes of the dramatic overflight on social media, said: "The plane flew over twice really low and at one point it seemed likely to crash."
Nuno Arroja adds: "I've surfied, and I really thought the plane was going to fall on my head."
