Half of the funeral services don't comply with regulations.
Half of funeral service providers do not comply with the legislation.
The Czech Trade Inspection Authority (ČOI) found out during inspections in the second quarter.
According to her, funeral services most often do not inform survivors of their prices or do not issue a written confirmation of receipt of the order.
The CTIA imposed 41 fines totalling 73,000 crowns.
Jiří Fröhlich, spokesperson, informed about this today.
Inspectors found misconduct at 47 out of 95 inspections.
In addition to non-information about prices and missing certificates, some funeral services have also sold products or provided services at prices other than those negotiated.
In five cases, the products sold were not properly labeled and once the seller used an officially unverified gauge.
Therefore, the inspection banned the sale of 23 products for a total of 7077 crowns.
It concerned urn wrappers, candle covers and vases that weren't properly marked with mandatory information.
"Due to the fact that there are still violations of the law in this specific area of services, the control action will continue in the next quarter of this year," Fröhlich added.
