They're younger people, not the older, grown-up teenagers getting into it.
Fopp, where almost one floor is currently reserved for gramophone records, has much more diverse visitors upon my arrival.
There are couples of seventies, tourists who take photos, teenagers and middle-aged women.
While the atmosphere isn't as relaxed as the stores used to be - the loudspeakers, instead of pulling jazz, echoes the latest pop from Wild Beasts full of synthesizers and sex, it's good to see different customers.
