It’s easy to listen to music on a computer or something like that, but gramophone records have their magic...,” he sighs eagerly.
I can't explain - it's unique.
My last stop is a store that supposedly inspired a new generation of gramophone record lovers: Urban Outfitters.
I'm pretending that I'm very biased by the calves of girls in tight jeans and I'm watching a group of teenage girls just clumping around Polaroid cameras, and then my father and daughter decide to buy a Crosley turntable.
There's a staircase on the left whose wall is obscured by Adele's gramophone records, Jeff Buckley, Amy Winehouse and Fleetwood Maca: a mixture of contemporary and classical music, the basis of any average collection of gramophone records.
No one looks at them - perhaps precisely because they are only for decoration and some of them are so high on the wall that they cannot be reached.
