It is far from her first restoration work in the Frýdlant region.
Thanks to it, for example, the stone elements of the facade in the rear tract of the Frýdlant Town Hall were restored, statues of St. Mary Magdalene in Zátiší, St. John of Nepomuk in Frýdlant, Piet in Frýdlantská Okružní Street, the Marian Column in Frýdlant or the Atlants in the facade of the spa in Nové Město pod Sm
The restoration of the tombstone of Melchiora, Kryštof and Kateřina from Redern began in Frýdlant in 2011.
Now the surface of the stone elements is purified from the build-up of impurities and crust, the loose stone parts are secured against falling and displacement; they will either anchor themselves to the wall or to each other.
They are also undergoing treatment and preservation of the surface.
Inscriptions on the tomb will be gilded again.
"It will then begin with the gilding of inscriptions on marble slabs with pure sliced gold," said Věra Sobotová, an official of the State Heritage Care of the Municipal Authority in Frýdlant.
From the past, there are no records that the tombstone has undergone any repairs.
On closer inspection, the holes, drilled in the marble columns.
They are hundreds of years old and are the remains after the tombstoire.
It was richly adorned, unfortunately after the raid of the Swedes during the Thirty Years War everything disappeared.
Literally combed the tombstone, Sobota noted.
In the Church of the Finding of the Holy Cross, restorers are at home with mild exaggeration.
After the flood in 2010, it was necessary to fix the tombstones, which found themselves under the water, the baptism, the murals in the tomb and now the tombstone were restored.
"We'd also like to get stained in the future," Sobota said.
The church is otherwise in very good condition, every year we put money into maintenance and repairs.
The restoration work on the restoration of the Redernov tombstone will come to a total of 128 thousand crowns.
They will be covered by subsidies, the city will not deposit any of its money into this part of the restoration.
One hundred thousand crowns will come from winning in the regional round of the competition Historical City of the Year 2015, the remaining 28 thousand crowns is the contribution of the Ministry of Culture, the mayor of Frýdlant Dan Ramzer said.
The council has decided to loosen the win to restore the tombstone.
