An Earthquake about Putin?
The Kremlin's ruler dismissed his loved one Ivanov.
On Friday, Russian President Vladimir Putin released Sergei Ivanov from the post of head of the presidential office.
Anton Vajno will take his place.
This was reported by Russian media, citing the Kremlin press service announcement.
In doing so, Putin has indicated that Ivanova is dismissed at his own request.
In a meeting carried by Rossiya 24, the president said he would meet Ivanov's wish when he took office, that he wanted to be the head of the presidential office for no more than four years.
At the same time, he announced that Ivanov would be his special representative for ecology and transport.
The news of the exchange at the head of the president's administration, now led by Ivanov's current representative Vajno, is considered quite surprising.
Ivanov, who is 63 years old, is described as one of Putin's closest collaborators.
In the past, for example, this former KGB officer has helded as defense minister and deputy prime minister.
He will now leave the chair of a member of the president's security council.
Ivanov, during a meeting with Putin, stated that the length of staying at the head of the administration of the head of the head of the state is actually a record holder.
He lasted four years and eight months.
In this context, he reminded that in the 25 years since its establishment, 11 people have already been relieved.
